══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
If you get 403 / permission denied errors, run this SQL
in your Supabase dashboard → SQL Editor:

-- Allow anyone (anon) to read bookings
CREATE POLICY "allow_select" ON bookings
  FOR SELECT TO anon USING (true);

-- Allow anyone to insert new bookings
CREATE POLICY "allow_insert" ON bookings
  FOR INSERT TO anon WITH CHECK (true);

-- Allow anyone to update bookings
CREATE POLICY "allow_update" ON bookings
  FOR UPDATE TO anon USING (true) WITH CHECK (true);

-- Enable RLS on the table if not already enabled
ALTER TABLE bookings ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

NOTE: For production, restrict these policies to authenticated
admin users for UPDATE and use service_role key server-side.
══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
